   168	    - Several solid orange rectangles overwrite that pattern as occluders.
   169	    - Each occluder has one nearby red or grey L triomino marker, where the triomino fills three cells of a 2x2 box.
   170	
   171	    Rule:
   172	    - Detect every orange filled rectangle and every red/grey L triomino.
   173	    - Read the triomino's missing-corner direction from the empty corner of its 2x2 box.
   174	    - For each grey triomino, follow that diagonal direction to the first orange rectangle and mark that rectangle for restoration.
   175	    - Infer the underlying 2x2 periodic blue/yellow tile from the visible background cells, repaint only the marked rectangles with the tile, and leave red-linked rectangles plus all triominoes unchanged.
   176	
   177	    Key insight:
